{"game_id":2026020262,"away":"CBJ","home":"BUF","split":{"name":"Monahan","side":0,"sec":2052},"lede":"Buffalo had last change, so Lindy Ruff picked most of these matchups. Buffalo played without Ryan McLeod and Louis Crevier. Columbus played without Ryan Lomberg and Luca Del Bel Belluz and lost Sean Monahan after 14:12 of the second.","notes":[{"kind":"match","head":"The third line drew Knies’s line","text":"Lindy Ruff sent Kulich, Norris and Zucker out for 5:11 of their 7:54 at 5-on-5 against Knies, Fantilli and Garland (66%, about 32% with no line matching), and the chances were close, 0.15 to 0.24 expected goals."},{"kind":"match","head":"The fourth line drew Voronkov’s line","text":"Malenstyn, Kozak and Carrick spent 4:01 of their 7:50 at 5-on-5 against Voronkov, Williams and Lorentz (51%, about 20% with no line matching)."},{"kind":"match","head":"Quinn’s line drew Coyle’s line","text":"Doan, Östlund and Quinn spent 4:37 of their 8:45 at 5-on-5 against Sillinger, Coyle and Olivier (53%, about 26% with no line matching), and the chances were close, 0.61 to 0.70 expected goals. Buffalo scored one of its five goals then."},{"kind":"swing","head":"One matchup paid off","text":"Benson, Krebs and Thompson kept drawing Columbus’s first line, Knies, Fantilli and Garland. In those 3:50 Buffalo had 0.35 expected goals to Columbus’s 0.00. Buffalo scored one of its five goals then."},{"kind":"exit","head":"After Monahan left, the lines changed but the matchups held","text":"Williams went from 17% to 27% and Lorentz from 16% to 24% of Columbus’s 5-on-5 time, and Garland dropped from 31% to 21%. The matchups stayed: the third line against Columbus’s first line (68% before, 61% after)."},{"kind":"result","head":"And it went better","text":"Columbus had 1.07 to 2.67 expected goals at 5-on-5 before Monahan left and 1.92 to 0.63 after. Columbus trailed for most of that stretch, though, and a team behind usually pushes the play, so the score explains part of it."}],"foot":"Lindy